# promise: #331
# The Little Window's "Open in" menu (the ⌄ and ⇧⌘O) as in Arc 1.172.1: 244 pt wide, 4 pt below the
# window's top and 4 pt in from its right edge, 46 pt rows in a list of at most 350 pt that scrolls,
# the space "Open in" names first and highlighted, shrinking to what the filter matches, "No results"
# in 64 pt. Before, Cra drew 54 pt rows, showed the first six spaces only, in sidebar order, flush with
# the window's top. Ten spaces here; little-window-one-space has the menu without a ⌄.
budget rss=700 stalls50=20
